comments[27]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-18T19:44:09.352Z",codex-agent,"Live evaluation is running sequentially on verified PUBLIC copies of pm-vcs and pm-lint. Twenty-four exact ground-truth aggregations; same installed local model in both arms; 4096 context, 96 output limit. Early results are negative: the small model copies context or requests excessive reads; budget refusals count as incorrect. No success claim is inferred from the architecture."
  "2026-10-18T19:59:55.257Z",codex-agent,"Measured npm run test:live: 24 exact questions from verified PUBLIC tracker copies (145 and 12 items; 814268 and 54941 JSON bytes), local gemma4-local:e2b-q3km, context 4096, output 96, temperature 0. RLM: 1/24 correct (4.17%), 35557 provider tokens total (1481.54/question), 82 model requests (3.42/question), 622384 ms total (25.93 s/question), 23 budget refusals. Truncated stuffing: 0/24 correct, 25225 tokens (1051.04/question), 24 requests (1/question), 117573 ms (4.90 s/question). One root per RLM question and no child calls. This does not demonstrate an RLM advantage. Public per-question metrics and response digests are in eval-results.json; README contains the table."
  "2026-10-18T21:16:44.464Z",codex-agent,"Calibration diagnosis: eval overrode defaults to 4096 context, 96 output tokens and 16000 run budget. Full read/partition payloads exceeded the next prompt, while output was too small for copying useful slices into spawn JSON. Add compact deterministic partition references in the model protocol, retain the exported lossless environment API, calibrate with synthetic two-partition/two-child tests, and measure without answer-based tuning. Eval will copy only a verified public revision and explicitly pin loopback Ollama transport."
  "2026-10-18T21:29:13.237Z",codex-agent,"Measured run is in progress with the small installed local model. The harness now records published source revision hashes, exact truth, compact partition reachability and model request counts, JSON answer scores, and response digests only. PM_RLM_LIVE_MODEL and PM_RLM_LIVE_BASE_URL are supported; external evaluation endpoints are rejected before inference."
  "2026-10-18T22:06:41.601Z",codex-agent,"Calibrated live eval completed successfully: 24 questions from public revisions pm-vcs f9283201108919939d0e1cfb489358c87ea8822b (145 items, 814268 JSON bytes) and pm-lint f2c20efa78139f4071f3dd08d317bea05337fe28 (12 items, 54941 bytes). Model gemma4-local:e2b-q3km, loopback Ollama, GPU execution observed, context 32768, output 512, budget 300000, depth 2, max calls 8. RLM 7/24 correct (29.17%), 339641 provider tokens total (14151.71/question), 254 requests (10.58/question), 1622475 ms total (67.60 seconds/question). Stuffing 2/24 (8.33%), 239974 tokens (9998.92/question), 24 requests (1/question), 1001191 ms (41.72 seconds/question). Eight RLM budget refusals; zero of 24 runs reached a child; 24 ledger roots total. Twelve truths are zero, so constant zero would score 12/24. No recursive aggregation quality or RLM advantage is established. README and eval-results.json retain provenance, truth and aggregates; raw responses are replaced by digests."
  "2026-10-18T22:06:46.044Z",codex-agent,"Eval isolation regression: copied workspace context 1024/output 32/budget 1000 reproduced inheritance with the prior helper (ERR_ASSERTION: 1024 != 32768). Explicit calibrated overrides now make the focused regression pass 1/1. Both published source settings have no rlm section, so the measured settings remained exactly 32768/512/300000; no answer-based tuning occurred. node test/revert.ts passed 7/7 isolated behavioral mutations, including this eval override, with exact source-byte restoration. PM_RLM_LIVE_MODEL and PM_RLM_LIVE_BASE_URL support future local capable-model reruns."
  "2026-10-18T23:28:41.326Z",codex-agent,"Seeded v2 design audited without inference using verified public revisions of pm-vcs (145 items) and pm-lint (12 items). Exactly 24 questions, 21 distinct answers, 13 numeric and 11 id-valued answers. Numeric range 0 through 12196. Histogram: answer 4 and ids pm-lint-8kis and pm-lint-trap each occur twice; all other 18 answers occur once. Most-common constant baseline 2/24 (8.33%); zero baseline 1/24 (4.17%). Selection uses only exact tracker truth and seed pm-rlm-balanced-v2, four numeric magnitude bands, id answers, and a per-source cap of two occurrences per answer. No new model calls. Previous measured results are labeled historical in README; exact new tasks and histogram are in docs/eval-design.json. Archive extraction now verifies every path and blob byte; attribute-bearing real Git regressions cover export-ignore and export-subst."
  "2026-10-18T23:31:52.441Z",codex-agent,"Revert proof: removing the answer-frequency cap makes the seeded distribution regression fail. Removing archive path-count validation changes the missing-path refusal and fails its diagnosis assertion; removing byte equality permits export-subst corruption and fails the real Git regression. All sources restored byte-for-byte. No model inference was run for this design audit."
  "2026-10-19T02:14:47.518Z",codex-agent,"Exactly one authorized cloud invocation completed all 24 pairs with glm-5.3:cloud, 131072 shared context allocation, 512 output allocation, temperature 0, existing 300000 charged-token budget, depth 2 and eight ledger calls. Source fingerprint matched before report generation. RLM: 0/24; 3511126 recorded tokens total, 146296.92 tokens/question; 183.78 seconds/question; 19.17 model requests/question; child reach 0/24. Stuffing: 0/24; 443318 recorded tokens total, 18471.58 tokens/question; 5.37 seconds/question; 1 request/question. RLM outer refusal histogram: budget 15, model/transport 9. Stuffing model/transport refusals: 8. RLM recorded 451 invalid-action refusals and zero delivered-read charge. Mean RLM charged/used/pending tokens: 151634.96/146296.92/5338.04. Pending reservations explain the difference; recorded responses settled to actual usage. Constant baselines: most-common answer 2/24 (8.33%), zero 1/24 (4.17%). No questions, prompts or settings were tuned during the run, and no further model calls were made. docs/EVAL-CLOUD.md, README and eval-results.json record exact results and limitations. This null result does not establish recursive aggregation quality or an RLM advantage."
  "2026-10-19T03:25:37.481Z",codex-agent,"Offline report regression uses saved synthetic measurements only: edited headings and misleading historical prose outside the marked region are preserved, a second report is byte-identical, and malformed/duplicate/reversed markers leave existing artifacts untouched. No live inference or measured-result artifact rewrite."
  "2026-10-19T03:31:18.487Z",codex-agent,"Revert evidence: restoring the historical-prose README locator fails the offline-report regression, which also proves rerun idempotence and no report writes on invalid marker structure. No model calls were made. Existing eval archive and seeded-design mutations also passed their revert proofs."
  "2026-10-19T04:32:36.455Z",codex-agent,"DJ8 and metric sweep: historical token provenance cannot be reconstructed per response. Reports now say reported-or-estimated, with explicit provenance for provider/fallback model counters, accounting charges, worst-case pending estimates and byte-estimated reads; scoring and observed counts are exact, timing is measured, allocations are configured limits. Run/tree summaries also label token usage. README, architecture, cloud report and artifact labels agree. Verified all pre-existing numeric values, rows, source revisions and measurement fingerprint unchanged; no live model calls."
  "2026-10-19T04:34:39.484Z",codex-agent,"Revert evidence: restoring the provider-only measurement description or table heading separately fails the offline report regression. Removing only the host tree token label fails native host JSON acceptance. Report regeneration remains idempotent under valid markers, with exact marker-failure exit 1 and no output writes on invalid markers. Historical numeric data is unchanged; provenance is intentionally reported-or-estimated because it was not retained per response."
  "2026-10-19T05:34:11.045Z",codex-agent,"Removed answer-format instructions from every generated question; JSON response requirements remain solely in the separate arm protocols. The seeded truth-only regression rejects any response-format instruction. README, cloud report and structured results explicitly invalidate the historical scores; the offline formatter preserves this notice. Historical rows, counters, timestamps, baselines and fingerprint are unchanged; no evaluation rerun."
  "2026-10-19T05:36:40.432Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proofs: restoring only the old bare-answer suffix fails the seeded format-neutral question assertion with exit 1; removing only the cloud invalidation notice fails the offline report regression with exit 1. Restoring both passes the linked 12/12 tests. Full revert suite passes 51/51. Compared the entire historical eval artifact against the previous commit: all existing data are deeply identical; only explicit invalidation metadata was added. No live eval was run."
  "2026-10-23T15:26:15.970Z",codex-agent,"STALE-CLAIM: audited main 09661846f4c24fd24d8effa2a7c578b3a5c49ed9; no open PR or recently pushed live branch references this record. Inspected: eval-results.json, docs/EVAL-CLOUD.md. Remaining: This item remains blocked by pm-rlm-kaht and the retained scores were explicitly invalidated by prompt-format asymmetry. Complete a valid independently authorized comparison; preserve historical measurements without claiming delivered evaluation. Release historical contention and retain real work as open; no delivery/cancellation is claimed."
  "2026-10-25T01:09:22.063Z",codex-agent,"Implement a public typed eval SDK and native CLI over immutable certified source copies. Keep both arms on the same local Ollama model, version exact questions and gold answers, retain failed attempts in accuracy and call counts, and label token provenance. Evaluation writes only to uniquely owned disposable SDK trackers; source corpus is read-only. Historical invalidated results remain unchanged. Validate no-git operation, competing evaluations, crash boundaries, and behavioral reverts before the CI release gates."
  "2026-10-25T01:13:28.355Z",codex-agent,"The typed evaluateRlm API and rlm eval command now bind frozen corpus hashes, use the same local-only model in both arms, preserve all refusals in the denominator, and emit compact summaries with opt-in rows. Evaluation controllers use the existing SDK-backed ledger lease, SDK lookup/create, and description compare-and-set transactions. No new deletion path exists. Interrupted reservations become explicit unknown metrics on rerun rather than duplicate inference; completed receipts are reused."
  "2026-10-25T01:23:27.753Z",codex-agent,"Public provenance verified for frozen pm-rlm and pm-lint revisions. The versioned suite has 24 format-neutral exact questions, including ownership, blockers, dependency paths and last-change timestamps. Local Ollama inventory was reachable, but Gemma generation exceeded 60 seconds and an independent minimal FunctionGemma probe exceeded 20 seconds without a response. The interrupted local trial is retained as pending evidence. The explicitly labeled constant-zero stub completed 24 paired public-data questions, 4/24 correct in both arms; these numbers validate harness mechanics, not model quality. Acceptance requiring a completed local-model comparison remains unmet, so the PR will be draft and this item remains in_progress."
  "2026-10-25T01:31:59.726Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proof: pm test pm-rlm-umh4 --run --only-last --progress --timeout 900 passed (one selected linked command, node test/evaluation-revert.ts). All 10/10 independent mutations produced targeted assertion failures with exit 1, then exact authored source bytes were restored: minimum question count, source digest, byte truncation, foreign skip reason, unknown failed-request usage, outer lease, description CAS, interrupted-arm no-retry, native no-git registration, and failed-child reach. Focused real-SDK tests passed 10/10 plus the dedicated failed-child test 1/1; typecheck, lint, docstrings and unchanged zero-duplication gate passed. Seven SIGKILL boundaries and seven competing boundary transitions use real non-git SDK trackers. Full npm/Bun release evidence is being collected in CI on PR 23."
  "2026-10-25T01:32:54.492Z",codex-agent,"Final public-data fallback validation: node test/evaluation-live.ts --stub completed 24 pairs on read-only copies of public pm-rlm (21 items, 236661 JSON bytes) and pm-lint (12 items, 54941 bytes). Both post-run corpus hashes match the versioned suite and the recorded implementation SHA-256 matches current measured source. Constant-zero stub: truncated 4/24, 190800 byte-estimated tokens, 24 calls, 1 ms arm time; recursive 4/24, 62303 byte-estimated tokens, 24 calls, 10420 ms arm time; zero children in both. All metrics are explicitly stub harness evidence. Live local-model acceptance remains pending after bounded inference timeouts; retain draft PR 23 and leave this item in_progress. SDK gap: no public-revision/archive attestation helper; preparation uses verified GitHub visibility/commit data plus Git blob comparison. Existing model counters do not retain per-response provider-versus-estimate provenance."
  "2026-10-25T01:36:35.881Z",codex-agent,"CI refinement: the existing shallow-clone proof inventory expected ten scripts; the new committed proof makes eleven. Updated that inventory, loaded the new erased type-contract module for vacuous coverage, covered malformed balanced JSON as an incomplete response, and removed a redundant optional-description branch by converting the selected SDK field to string before parsing. Focused validation passed 2/2. The additional malformed-response classification mutation failed its targeted assertion with exit 1 and restored exact source bytes; evaluation-revert.ts now contains 11 independent proofs (the original ten already passed through the linked pm runner). Final implementation-bound read-only stub validation retains 4/24 in both arms, 190800 versus 62303 byte-estimated tokens, 24 calls each, and 1 versus 12660 ms arm time. Source hashes remained unchanged. Final npm and Bun gates will run on the pushed head."
  "2026-10-25T01:37:32.964Z",codex-agent,"Packed acceptance now explicitly includes the evaluation documentation and suite/result JSON in its existing file allowlist. Both real npm and Bun consumers execute the exported evaluateRlm API against their non-git SDK trackers with an explicitly labeled deterministic stub, verify compact receipts and id reuse, discover the eval command, and exercise its typed configuration refusal through the installed native host. This runs in the CI release gate, alongside the complete shallow-clone revert suite; unchanged source coverage thresholds remain 100 in all four dimensions."
  "2026-10-25T01:45:38.525Z",codex-agent,"Final SDK consistency refinement: evaluateRlm now captures declarations, including nested source maps and settings, before its first await while preserving the transport and boundary-hook objects. The targeted SDK test mutates the original id, model, mode and source map during IO and passes 1/1 with the fix; removing only the deep capture fails an assertion with exit 1 and restores exact source. The committed evaluation proof script now contains twelve independent behavioral mutations. Refreshed final read-only public-data stub artifact matches the measured implementation fingerprint: both arms remain 4/24 with 24 calls and zero children; truncated 190800 byte-estimated tokens and 1 ms, recursive 62303 and 12560 ms. Exact-head full CI and packed npm/Bun acceptance will be linked in the draft PR. Local strict health additionally reports extension_host_pm_cli_version_skew for pinned CLI 2026.10.20 versus global pm-github 2026.10.24; clean CI health is the relevant isolated evidence. No dependency or global setting was changed."
  "2026-10-25T02:03:06.401Z",codex-agent,"Local inference availability recovered during the CI wait: a fresh minimal FunctionGemma request completed in roughly four seconds after earlier bounded timeouts. Starting the frozen 24-question live comparison with the installed functiongemma:270m model in both arms, selected only for availability. Questions, gold, source revisions, context/output allocations and engine limits are unchanged. Preserve failures and unknown usage honestly; no answer-based tuning or advantage claim."
  "2026-10-25T02:13:04.285Z",codex-agent,"Acceptance live comparison completed: one frozen 24-question trial on verified public pm-rlm (21 items, 236661 JSON bytes) and pm-lint (12 items, 54941 bytes), using the same installed local functiongemma:270m transport for both arms. Context 8192, output 256, temperature zero; native limits 60000 charged tokens, depth two, four logical nodes. Truncated: 0/24 exact, 53125 reported-or-estimated model tokens, 24 observed requests, 28542 ms arm wall time, no outer refusals. Recursive engine: 0/24, 521496 tokens, 384 requests, 386805 ms, 24 budget refusals, zero children. No transport failures; all refusals remain in the denominator. Constant zero scores 4/24. This does not establish useful answer quality, child quality or an RLM advantage. Read-only source post-run hashes and measured implementation fingerprint match. docs/public-eval-results.json and docs/PUBLIC-EVALUATION.md retain every paired observation and methodology; historical invalidated artifacts are unchanged. The PR can leave draft after this live result is committed, with final artifact-head CI still required. Item remains in_progress for orchestrator verification."
  "2026-10-26T08:25:22.661Z",codex-agent,"Owner-decision correction: PR #23 merged as 73a7176bba9820a9055b40f8b10622bb817b4928 at 2026-10-25T02:44:07Z and delivers the evaluation harness, not an accepted recursive-quality result. Inspected src/evaluation.ts and existing evaluation receipts: functiongemma:270m scored 0/24 for both arms and reached no children under the recursive budget. The orchestrator requires this item OPEN pending the owner decision on that result. Reuse existing Task pm-rlm-8xxq for the 9B rerun rather than create a duplicate. No inference is run by this closure sweep."
